# **`-f` folds to upper case, not to lower**, and the difference shows only
# beside punctuation: folding down puts `[` (91) below `a` (97), folding up puts
# it above `Z` (90). The tool answers `ab`, `Zb`, `[a`.
#
# Found the same way as the case above and by the same half of the sweep: three
# README files in this repository begin lines with `**[`, and the generated
# alphabet was letters and digits.
args: -f
input:
[a
Zb
ab
